.\"
.\" EXIT(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH EXIT 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
exit, _exit \- terminate the calling process
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdlib.h>
.PP
.BI "void exit(int " status ");
.BI "void _exit(int " status ");
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR exit ()
function terminates the calling process immediately, returning
.I status
to the parent process.
.PP
The low-order 8 bits of
.I status
are available to the parent process via
.BR wait (2)
or
.BR waitpid (2).
.SH RETURN VALUE
These functions do not return.
.SH ERRORS
None.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 1 (SYS_EXIT)
Arguments:      status (on stack)

    push status
    push $0
    mov eax, 1
    int $0x80
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wait (2),
.BR waitpid (2),
.BR fork (2),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008.
